    '## Tie, cushion and selected-unit arithmetic','',
    'For pair volume`T_u`, A share`s_u`, state pair total`T`and net`M=ΣT_u(2s_u−1)`, the unbounded shift to target fractional pair margin`g`is`(g−M/T)/2`. Thus `(B−A)/(2(A+B))`ties; pair A+1adds0.5**share** points. A+1share point adds2pair-margin points and`.02*T_u`net votes. The legal plurality, net votes, pair-margin denominator and all-candidate denominator remain separate.','',
    f'At2024county weights, pair total5,511,942and net+613,784give tie{float(base["shift_share_pp"]):+.6f}share points and pair A+1{float(baseplus["shift_share_pp"]):+.6f}points, targeting55,119.42net votes. An all-candidate A+1cushion targets56,333.10net votes and needs{float(baseall["shift_share_pp"]):+.6f}points instead. At finer native weights the corresponding **bounded** shifts are{float(native["shift_share_pp"]):+.6f}and{float(nativeplus["shift_share_pp"]):+.6f}; clipping means their difference is not exactly0.5points. Unbounded values remain separate in the outputs. We solve `ΣT_u[2clip(s_u+δ,0,1)−1]=gT`; every resulting unit share is within[0,1]. [State scenarios](data/baselines/state-scenarios.csv), [settings](data/baselines/scenario-settings.json), [calculator](data/baselines/calculator.py). Historical weights: '+link('sos-2024-president-csv','ISBE native records')+'.','',
    'Each [native target row](data/baselines/native-target-scenarios.csv.gz) retains observed A/B, source positions, source-derived weight, baseline contribution, target contribution, net gain, +1share-point gain and selected-unit-only requirement. There are90,558rows:all10,062contexts×3historical volume settings×3targets. Administrative contexts remain unavailable observations with no assigned pair pool. [Authority targets](data/baselines/authority-target-scenarios.csv) retain all108disjoint authorities and [county targets](data/baselines/county-target-scenarios.csv.gz) retain all102combined counties. No priority filter enters state arithmetic. Native/authority all-named denominators remain unavailable; only the explicitly stated statewide historical all-candidate denominator supplies that illustrative cushion.','',
    'For one selected unit, every other unit stays at the model baseline with0additional share shift: `q=(T_u+gT−M_other)/(2T_u)`. Negative requirements mean already secured, above1impossible, and no positive pool remains a separate state. Threshold equality is a tie benchmark. It is not a uniquely necessary target for each unit; gains and losses can offset across the complete state. The CLI allows an explicit clipped other-unit shift.','',
